(5607918, 811405, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from the CC CLub!!!!<br/> <br/>Well, I am not sure what the closet of doom is, but I think I may have several of them in this house.  Mostly under my kids beds!!!<br/> <br/>I like your idea of an overflowing glass.  I think what killed your shot here, was the darkness.  Because the glass is black you would need a fairly bright light to see what is going on in the shot. Maybe a little more spot metering would have helped with the light.  In Post processing, adjusting the exposure may have light it a bit more and then playing with brightness and contrast, but I still think this would have been fairly dark<br/> <br/>Now if I tilt my screen, I can see your shot fairly well.  <br/> <br/>Your high ISO is giving off a lot of grain, you are a little tilted as well and the bottom bit of the glass is cut off and out of focus.  <br/> <br/>But the focus on the oil pouring in and the top of the glass is sharp.  Your shot is very centered, maybe having only half of the glass showing on the right with the oil pouring out of it, would have given you more depth and POV. <br/> <br/>I would retake this shot and see what you can do , cos I think with the black glass it could be stunning!</td>', 'Hi from the CC CLub!!!! Well, I am not sure what the closet of doom is, but I think I may have several of them in this house.  Mostly under my kids beds!!! I like your idea of an overflowing glass.  I think what killed your shot here, was the darkness.  Because the glass is black you would need a fairly bright light to see what is going on in the shot. Maybe a little more spot metering would have helped with the light.  In Post processing, adjusting the exposure may have light it a bit more and then playing with brightness and contrast, but I still think this would have been fairly dark Now if I tilt my screen, I can see your shot fairly well.   Your high ISO is giving off a lot of grain, you are a little tilted as well and the bottom bit of the glass is cut off and out of focus.   But the focus on the oil pouring in and the top of the glass is sharp.  Your shot is very centered, maybe having only half of the glass showing on the right with the oil pouring out of it, would have given you more depth and POV.  I would retake this shot and see what you can do , cos I think with the black glass it could be stunning!', '2009-08-11 21:27:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5607942, 810367, 87808, '<td valign="top">CC Club here!!<br/> <br/>I had to study your shot and read your description several times before I understood what was happening. It is a very clever photo. <br/> <br/>Unfortunately your second olive looks like it is a shadow of the first, which is a shame.. Your first olive is so centered, cropping a little would have helped with the perception.<br/> <br/>If this was not an oil challenge I am not sure people would have got that it is in fact olives.  <br/> <br/>Play around with angles,</td>', 'CC Club here!! I had to study your shot and read your description several times before I understood what was happening. It is a very clever photo.  Unfortunately your second olive looks like it is a shadow of the first, which is a shame.. Your first olive is so centered, cropping a little would have helped with the perception. If this was not an oil challenge I am not sure people would have got that it is in fact olives.   Play around with angles,', '2009-08-11 21:58:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5607951, 811575, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hi from teh Cc Club, <br/> <br/>Okay, not fair!! What am I supposed to say about a fabulous shot!!!<br/> <br/>Seriously, the only thing I can see is that it is a little tilted!<br/> <br/>that is IT<br/> <br/>I think this is a great shot, well done a the placement</td>', 'Hi from teh Cc Club,  Okay, not fair!! What am I supposed to say about a fabulous shot!!! Seriously, the only thing I can see is that it is a little tilted! that is IT I think this is a great shot, well done a the placement', '2009-08-11 22:02:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5607960, 811422, 87808, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club. <br/> <br/>For your first ever submission this is pretty good.<br/> <br/>I think that there are several things about this shot that could be worked on.  <br/> <br/>A tighter crop would have helped this shot a little more.  You have more plate on the bottom than at the top and the rest of flower is out of focus towards the top with a tiny piece of plate showing. <br/> <br/>A different or deeper coloured oil would have made the oil or sunflower stand out more.  <br/> <br/>You are tack sharp and the focus is excellent on the flower. Your lighting is good as it brings out the true colours of the sunflower. <br/> <br/>In post processing, maybe try flipping it around to see if that make the POV more pleasing. <br/> <br/>I am looking forward to seeing more from you!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club.  For your first ever submission this is pretty good. I think that there are several things about this shot that could be worked on.   A tighter crop would have helped this shot a little more.  You have more plate on the bottom than at the top and the rest of flower is out of focus towards the top with a tiny piece of plate showing.  A different or deeper coloured oil would have made the oil or sunflower stand out more.   You are tack sharp and the focus is excellent on the flower. Your lighting is good as it brings out the true colours of the sunflower.  In post processing, maybe try flipping it around to see if that make the POV more pleasing.  I am looking forward to seeing more from you! ', '2009-08-11 22:08:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(5608129, 811509, 47933, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Good concept. Can''t add much about the compression that hasn''t already been said. <br/> <br/>Lighting is good. The capsules are overall a little soft as 2.8 is a bit much for this shot. Keeping the 100 ISO you might want to try f8-f11 and a tripod.</td>', 'Critique Club Good concept. Can''t add much about the compression that hasn''t already been said.  Lighting is good. The capsules are overall a little soft as 2.8 is a bit much for this shot. Keeping the 100 ISO you might want to try f8-f11 and a tripod.', '2009-08-11 23:46:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5608240, 811568, 72103, '<td valign="top">Very original, well shot!</td>', 'Very original, well shot!', '2009-08-12 00:31:07.000000', NULL, 0),
